  "term": "anthropomorphism",
  "definition": "Anthropomorphism is the tendency to assume that things very different from humans, especially gods or natural forces, have human qualities. In historical psychology, it is described as a more limited idea than animism because it specifically involves giving a human-like form or character to what is being understood.",
